+/* A kept static layer (perf, additive). plat_layer_begin(key, y0, y1)
+ * returns 1 when the platform will keep a layer: screen rows y0..y1-1 are
+ * then cleared to "nothing"; the caller draws the layer (plat_rect /
+ * plat_checker / spans only, no index 0) and calls plat_layer_end(), which
+ * keeps exactly the pixels drawn since begin (the rows are left
+ * undefined: the caller redraws what lies under the layer). Later,
+ * plat_layer_restore(key) draws those pixels again (the rest of the rows
+ * is left alone, so the layer is transparent where it drew nothing) and
+ * returns 1, or 0 when that layer is not held (any may be dropped at any
+ * time). Weak defaults (core/src/ui_raster.c): begin and restore return 0.
+ * GBA: rects in its spare EWRAM block. */
+int  plat_layer_begin(uint32_t key, int y0, int y1);
+void plat_layer_end(void);
+int  plat_layer_restore(uint32_t key);
 
